[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m Find the greatest common divisor of $3339$, $2961$, and $1491$.
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of $3339$, $2961$, and $1491$, we can use the Euclidean algorithm. The Euclidean algorithm is an efficient method for computing the greatest common divisor (GCD) of two numbers. It is based on the principle that the GCD of two numbers also divides their difference.
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m Here are the steps to find the GCD of $3339$, $2961$, and $1491$ using the Euclidean algorithm:
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m 1. Divide $3339$ by $2961$ and find the remainder.
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m    3339 \div 2961 = 1 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 378
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m    So, $3339 = 2961 \cdot 1 + 378$.
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m 2. Now, divide $2961$ by $378$ and find the remainder.
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m    2961 \div 378 = 7 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 105
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m    So, $2961 = 378 \cdot 7 + 105$.
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m 3. Next, divide $378$ by $105$ and find the remainder.
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m    378 \div 105 = 3 \quad \text{remainder} \quad 0
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m    So, $378 = 105 \cdot 3 + 0$.
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m Since the remainder is now $0$, the GCD is the last non-zero remainder, which is $105$.
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m Therefore, the greatest common divisor of $3339$, $2961$, and $1491$ is $\boxed{105}$.<|endoftext|>
