[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m A robot moving forward at a constant speed takes 2.5 hours to travel 1 kilometer. Moving forward at this same constant speed, it takes the robot 90 seconds to travel the length of a particular hallway. How many meters long is the hallway?
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m To find the length of the hallway, we first need to determine the robot's speed. We know that the robot takes 2.5 hours to travel 1 kilometer. Since there are 3600 seconds in an hour, we can calculate the speed as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m Speed = Distance / Time
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m Speed = 1 kilometer / 2.5 hours
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m Speed = 400 meters per hour
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m Now that we know the robot's speed, we can calculate the length of the hallway. We know that the robot takes 90 seconds to travel the length of the hallway. Since there are 3600 seconds in an hour, we can convert the time to hours:
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m 90 seconds / 3600 seconds per hour = 0.025 hours
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m Now we can calculate the length of the hallway using the speed we just calculated:
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m Length of the hallway = Speed * Time
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m Length of the hallway = 400 meters per hour * 0.025 hours
[36m(main_task pid=588366)[0m Length of the hallway = 10 meters
